        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-37905/blocks/prose-page-004",
      "source": "sections/page-004.md",
      "source_hash": "b8fc4d944e922eb6135e64f106cbff87aed98134db08b31a2eb178e7e80e35c3",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "A blank page with no extracted text.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-37905/blocks/prose-page-005",
      "source": "sections/page-005.md",
      "source_hash": "eec9194cb8cda02b78a45c88adbb3b76df61d628a525cd1b4e3a99a34863b51e",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "The preface explains that the guidelines highlight key principles for accelerating immunization programmes and will need regular updating. It states that they supplement, rather than replace, the EPI training materials and mentions a related UNICEF issue paper.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-37905/blocks/prose-page-006",
      "source": "sections/page-006.md",
      "source_hash": "b8fc4d944e922eb6135e64f106cbff87aed98134db08b31a2eb178e7e80e35c3",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "A blank page with no extracted text.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-37905/blocks/prose-page-007",
      "source": "sections/page-007.md",
      "source_hash": "a9931925325cab149041a8bcbc8210622cfcf398b1c85a6630333a67d1061ac2",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Opens the introduction, noting that with 1990 approaching only about a third of children in developing countries outside China receive a third dose of polio and DTP vaccines. It argues that political will to raise coverage is not hard to mobilize, as leaders welcome promises of protecting children cheaply.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-37905/blocks/prose-page-008",
      "source": "sections/page-008.md",
      "source_hash": "17a735ce5f9684ec712a2557adc6d5be9925e38831821d5fec1f61c46d7845de",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Notes that national immunization days have proved an effective way of using political will to raise coverage and that UNICEF and WHO will promote a global goal. It stresses reaching children early because EPI diseases strike young, such as pertussis deaths in the first six months.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-37905/blocks/prose-page-009",
      "source": "sections/page-009.md",
      "source_hash": "df46dfa59b95f2800e3fc90133faf6a585e411283213f2f37c48bcc8c10d5b49",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Explains vaccine timing, with measles vaccine delayed to nine months, oral polio from birth and DTP from six weeks, and advises a minimum four-week interval between doses. It stresses registering and tracking newborns so that older at-risk children cease to be a problem.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-37905/blocks/prose-page-010",
      "source": "sections/page-010.md",
      "source_hash": "66e6ee37fb08734e95c5188c32af052db2c84c155a1be8dcaf76a4d90b33abc0",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Opens the section on planning acceleration, stressing that plans must cover at least three years rather than a single immunization day. It recommends joint national and international technical reviews of one to three weeks to draw up an acceleration plan.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-37905/blocks/prose-page-011",
      "source": "sections/page-011.md",
      "source_hash": "9ec2c6bf1cfbf916cc252cf0a05d39e6ff451f2dc3577d54396bfb9b9669e809",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Advises that joint planning reviews should precede political commitment to a detailed strategy, with WHO and UNICEF able to provide consultants. It notes the time needed for different strategies and the need for rapid communication so problems reach those who can solve them.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-37905/blocks/prose-page-012",
      "source": "sections/page-012.md",
      "source_hash": "072143b2b73dcd03d29d2e3c4083493314da4d1879fc5acb5c5694d6af5a8871",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes the careful planning needed for social mobilization, with messages and channels chosen for each group whose support is needed. It warns that vaccine supplies require long lead times, citing a case where a promised delivery was met only by diverting vaccines from other countries.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-37905/blocks/prose-page-013",
      "source": "sections/page-013.md",
      "source_hash": "31f2582f02f3b18e485866f970b5e2f866666aca16aba985cc22354449538c9e",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Recommends confirming vaccine supply at least four months before fixing an immunization day, and allowing time for training and logistics. It says plans for sustainable programmes should be realistic about government and external contributions over several years.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-37905/blocks/prose-page-014",
      "source": "sections/page-014.md",
      "source_hash": "01d4bc02a27edaa8b60045ffd11803657044dbbfa4d2b725a8fb227351d5b385",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "States that the long-term aim is national financial and technical self-sufficiency and that ways to accelerate programmes are often complementary. It introduces acceleration through improving existing primary health care services, which can quickly raise measles and third-dose coverage.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-37905/blocks/prose-page-015",
      "source": "sections/page-015.md",
      "source_hash": "5b90ac70f82ff7613d603707ecceca1251ea6ce37516e8434761fa070ff81171",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Lists ways to strengthen existing services, such as better training, supervision and logistics, shorter waiting times and not refusing children with minor illness or malnutrition. It gives examples of community-based tracking of children in Colombia and Madras.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-37905/blocks/prose-page-016",
      "source": "sections/page-016.md",
      "source_hash": "1131a535e1363b934520f2727352082f059cd33e63a5f47a91beca35d0a8a8a5",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Notes that schools are an underused resource, citing health education in Abidjan and Bombay that encouraged parents to vaccinate younger siblings. It begins a list of priority actions, starting with offering immunization at every health contact.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-37905/blocks/prose-page-017",
      "source": "sections/page-017.md",
      "source_hash": "62be5e4db53ac7fa3044c8dea0d45b1281267d43be66bcebb1352c99a1676b1e",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Continues the priority actions, including reducing drop-out between first and last doses through community involvement, convenient services and tracing defaulters. It also calls for higher priority for measles vaccination, which helps raise DTP and polio coverage.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-37905/blocks/prose-page-018",
      "source": "sections/page-018.md",
      "source_hash": "77f7cef755a4a28afa38f7962986356f5b219c800d9789b4ebc4570b3106c502",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Discusses polio as a feared disease already declining under EPI and neonatal tetanus as a neglected disease causing about a million deaths a year. It also flags low coverage in urban slums as cities grow.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-37905/blocks/prose-page-019",
      "source": "sections/page-019.md",
      "source_hash": "b098809c9d6132dd75e9675ce25b5a3d686a0d3bfa7c943551abab4a34d6fa7b",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Notes barriers to immunizing urban slum populations and urges priority for accessible services there. It opens the section on national immunization days, which have rapidly raised coverage where backed by strong political commitment.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-37905/blocks/prose-page-020",
      "source": "sections/page-020.md",
      "source_hash": "36a972366b97e6b2737f8547ee8ed97b6da2cb3ddb0ba12d4662e63b46dd6d46",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Explains that successful national immunization days need careful planning of vaccine supply, volunteer training and publicity, plus personal involvement of top political leaders. It warns of risks, chiefly sustainability, and that mass efforts tend to reach older children rather than the youngest at greatest risk.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-37905/blocks/prose-page-021",
      "source": "sections/page-021.md",
      "source_hash": "6f8bcb622dbdc9bd8948e8b282726b3b3adf3b0b59d6fac986218fcde16ccd4c",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Advises that political support for national days should become a national goal that outlasts individuals and parties, and that health staff must be fully committed. It raises the need to decide age groups and record-keeping for campaign strategies.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-37905/blocks/prose-page-022",
      "source": "sections/page-022.md",
      "source_hash": "3e1216d934cc2344db0bda2a1fe467b31df4ec43b83ca4fbfa1aa7091dfcee2c",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Stresses careful records to avoid giving too many or too few doses, a general upper age limit and minimum ages for DTP and measles vaccine. It suggests using volunteers to register target children before a campaign.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-37905/blocks/prose-page-023",
      "source": "sections/page-023.md",
      "source_hash": "393571b28c5f7bd8b7d6eae16bd4077f090e80c924a945338bb655e1dbde8ed3",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Advises finishing registration about two months ahead to finalize logistics, or estimating populations where that is impossible, and cautions about over-immunizing women with tetanus toxoid. It describes national immunization days as a catalytic step.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-37905/blocks/prose-page-024",
      "source": "sections/page-024.md",
      "source_hash": "3e0d5bf05bd690d69aeefff6f0a2144138c7e62f3ca12984d99ebb9d70110180",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Says national days should support the long-term strategy of integrating immunization with maternal and child health services. It opens the section on social mobilization as the keystone of acceleration, applicable to all approaches.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-37905/blocks/prose-page-025",
      "source": "sections/page-025.md",
      "source_hash": "1474d9ffd87c0cd9e8972e093e92cee879dea1c8bc151e84354e4869141f2a94",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Lists forms of social mobilization, from political leaders and celebrities to mass media, community action and health education, as complementary approaches. It then introduces evaluation of acceleration activities, stressing the need for objective data.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-37905/blocks/prose-page-026",
      "source": "sections/page-026.md",
      "source_hash": "ba36c6821be4cca83b1b1ad2cce213b6340f6bccb71af8d56c3d7a437d1cd939",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Explains that publicity around national days makes subjective judgements unreliable, so coverage surveys using the EPI cluster sampling method and trends in disease incidence are priority data. It lists evaluation questions on what worked and what problems arose.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-37905/blocks/prose-page-027",
      "source": "sections/page-027.md",
      "source_hash": "128168311017df05059f00f3f431da76bfaf077b24cf36847bc426ac6faf2c97",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Completes the list of evaluation questions on resources, communication, costs and links to routine services, then opens the conclusion on planning and strengthening primary health care.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-37905/blocks/prose-page-028",
      "source": "sections/page-028.md",
      "source_hash": "965636eedd23c9159894a65d5ee91485ab66bd62daf48407ab43be4c3c789b01",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "The conclusion says acceleration should improve the quality of existing services, with training, supervision and community participation, and that national days must support lasting services. It begins a checklist of requirements, such as a schedule allowing three doses at four-week intervals.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-37905/blocks/prose-page-029",
      "source": "sections/page-029.md",
      "source_hash": "94d02406c04dcd3406e4620b6bf65de952cbabe0f3e05870cd51095da2704779",
      "narrative": [
        {
